p.src:
The transcript of the film clip is noisy in detail, but its structure is clear enough. A set of possible children is screened, compared, and selected. Sex can be chosen. The issue is no longer simply whether to have a child, but which child to have. In compact form, $\text{screening} + \text{parental preference}
\Longrightarrow
\text{selection among possible children}.$ That is the reason this section appears where it does. Sandel wants us to feel, before he names it outright, the slide from healing to choosing, from accepting a child to selecting among candidates.

